    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d761">

                <pb facs="0906" n="804" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg804"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.6711/190: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crosby</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-05-25T15:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 25, 1927—3
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 5:13 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>40. I have just returned from an informal call on Nusret Bey.<anchor n="45"
                        xml:id="d761-f1"/> Under instructions from Angora he asked me to telegraph
                    the Department requesting <hi rendition="#italic">agrément</hi> of Mouhtar Bey
                    as the Ambassador of Turkey in the United States. Mouhtar Bey has had an
                    extended diplomatic service. He has served as Foreign Minister in the Cabinet of
                    Rao Bey, Minister in Athens, and Ambassador in Russia; and at the present time
                    he is a Deputy from Constantinople. I regret that he is not known to me
                    personally.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crosby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d761-f1" n="45" xml:id="d761-f1-content">
                <p>Delegate at Constantinople of the Turkish Foreign Minister.</p>
            </note>
